      "Abstract",
      "Introduction",
      "Study cohort",
      "A single-cell atlas of meningioma reveals recurrent transcriptional metaprograms",
      "Myeloid cell states are differentially enriched across existing biological classifications",
      "Some myeloid MPs are consistent with myeloid gene programs from glioblastoma",
      "Bulk proteomic analysis validates the biological correlates of myeloid MPs",
      "Some meningiomas exhibit considerable neoplastic transcriptional heterogeneity over space",
      "Neoplastic chromosome 1p and 22q losses are largely stable across whole meningiomas",
      "Bulk methylation validates the regional consistency in meningioma biomarkers",
      "Chromosome 22q and 1p loss incurs greater spatial neoplastic heterogeneity",
      "Spatially informed sampling provides insight into the immune reprogramming of meningioma",
      "The myeloid TNF MP is suppressed across the dura–tumor interface",
      "Myeloid–neoplastic interactions are state-specific and influence the tumor microenvironment",
      "Spatial transcriptomics reveals global spatial dependencies between cell types",
      "Meningioma cell states are prognostic, independent of MG and cell abundance",
      "Integrating meningioma cell states can refine outcome predictions in addition to existing MGs",
